2026-09-26T08:54:27.1617847Z     
2026-09-26T08:54:27.1618011Z     The ``pytest`` framework makes it easy to write small tests, yet
2026-09-26T08:54:27.1618228Z     scales to support complex functional testing for applications and libraries.
2026-09-26T08:54:27.1618312Z     
2026-09-26T08:54:27.1618413Z     An example of a simple test:
2026-09-26T08:54:27.1618497Z     
2026-09-26T08:54:27.1618606Z     .. code-block:: python
2026-09-26T08:54:27.1618689Z     
2026-09-26T08:54:27.1618790Z         # content of test_sample.py
2026-09-26T08:54:27.1618880Z         def inc(x):
2026-09-26T08:54:27.1618979Z             return x + 1
2026-09-26T08:54:27.1619054Z     
2026-09-26T08:54:27.1619137Z     
2026-09-26T08:54:27.1619238Z         def test_answer():
2026-09-26T08:54:27.1619332Z             assert inc(3) == 5
2026-09-26T08:54:27.1619419Z     
2026-09-26T08:54:27.1619504Z     
2026-09-26T08:54:27.1619599Z     To execute it::
2026-09-26T08:54:27.1619684Z     
2026-09-26T08:54:27.1619774Z         $ pytest
2026-09-26T08:54:27.1619937Z         ============================= test session starts =============================
2026-09-26T08:54:27.1620026Z         collected 1 items
2026-09-26T08:54:27.1620109Z     
2026-09-26T08:54:27.1620209Z         test_sample.py F
2026-09-26T08:54:27.1620284Z     
2026-09-26T08:54:27.1620432Z         ================================== FAILURES ===================================
2026-09-26T08:54:27.1620611Z         _________________________________ test_answer _________________________________
2026-09-26T08:54:27.1620693Z     
2026-09-26T08:54:27.1620787Z             def test_answer():
2026-09-26T08:54:27.1620888Z         >       assert inc(3) == 5
2026-09-26T08:54:27.1620991Z         E       assert 4 == 5
2026-09-26T08:54:27.1621086Z         E        +  where 4 = inc(3)
2026-09-26T08:54:27.1621167Z     
